  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Recovery and Resilience (CRR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to develop a methodology to identify individuals formerly associated with or affected by Non-State Armed Groups who are either trapped in securitized state responses or have self-reintegrated into communities. A key focus is on survivors of sexual violence whose needs remain unmet under current DDR, development, and stabilization approaches. By devising a sensitive and confidential identification process, qualitative research will be conducted in Mayo-Sava, Mayo-Tsanaga, and Lo</narrative>
  </description>
